-baseline gap-2.5 text-sm md:text-base font-heading font-semibold text-text-primary uppercase tracking-[0.06em]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-block rounded-sm px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.16em] self-center\",\"style\":{\"color\":\"#4dc9f6\",\"background\":\"#4dc9f61a\",\"border\":\"1px solid #4dc9f640\"},\"children\":\"Legend\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankCardH3\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Eudora\",\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L40\",null,{\"href\":\"/tier-list?rank=legend\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-text-accent hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankTierListLink\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}],\" →\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-muted text-[13px] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceLead\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\",\"name\":\"Eudora\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"50.80\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Eudora\",\"delta\":\"-0.07%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"1.86\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"60.03\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[\"$La0\",\"$La1\",\"$La2\"]}],\"$La3\",\"$La4\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Eudora is not a \\\"burst mage\\\". She is one passive that doubles as her entire ceiling. Superconductor, the 5-second debuff her skills apply on hit after the 2.1.88 buff, is the only reason to lock her over Aurora, Cyclops, or Vale. Every skill in her kit deals normal damage on first contact. Every skill in her kit deals real damage when it lands on a Superconductor-marked target.\"}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"That is the whole hero. The order matters because of the math. S2 (Ball Lightning) marks AND stuns at the same instant, which means the moment a target is marked they are also locked in place. Your S1 then fires into a stationary target with the bonus damage applied, and your ultimate calls down a follow-up area strike on the same spot. You lose this entire windfall if you open with S1 on an unmarked enemy. The base S1 damage hits, the Superconductor bonus does not, and your S2 stun is now landing on a target who watched the lightning come from across the lane.\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Every other character note about Eudora flows from this. Her flat S1 cooldown is not so you can spam wave clear. It is so the bonus is available on the next cast after S2. The 2.1.88 chain reduction changes the ceiling: when the delayed chain damage from a Superconductor-triggered S1 fires, it now cuts S1's cooldown by half the skill's cooldown rather than a flat 1.5 seconds. That makes a second S1 mark inside a single teamfight realistic rather than a theoretical luxury. Her long ultimate cooldown is acceptable because the area follow-up after a marked hit makes it a teamfight nuke, not a single-target gimmick.\"}]\n81:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Laning: the first 5 minutes\"]}]\n82:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Take S1 first and clear the first wave from max range.\"}],\" Forked Lightning is fan-shaped now. You can hit the entire melee wave and graze the ranged minions from outside the enemy mid laner's auto-attack range. Do this twice and you are level 3 with their wave still pushing toward you.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Save S2 for the first time the enemy mid laner takes a step forward.\"}],\" Not for last hits, not for poke. The opponent will eventually push too far for a wave clear, and that is your kill window. Mark them with S2, animation-cancel into S1, and chain the ult. If they survive, they burned their escape, which is the same as a kill for the next stretch of the game.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Never walk into the river before level 4.\"}],\" Eudora has zero mobility before Flicker is up. The enemy jungler watches mid lane for exactly this reason: a level-2 Eudora pushing for a vision ward is the easiest kill on the map. Stay behind your second tower until your ult is online or your jungler is in your river quadrant.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n83:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The power spike you are farming toward\"]}]\n84:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"The spike is \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Genius Wand into Holy Crystal\"}],\". Genius Wand drops at the 6-to-7 minute mark with average mid-lane farm and immediately gives you 75 magic power plus a stacking Magic-defense reduction: every skill hit cuts the target's Magic Defense for 2 seconds, stacking up to 3 times. Two skills on a target strip enough magic defense that your next mark starts threatening squishy lanes outright. This is the spike that lets you start hunting side lanes between waves.\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Holy Crystal lands around the 11-to-12 minute mark. The 21-to-35 percent extra magic power scaling on top of 165 base magic power is the single largest damage bump in Eudora's build. Before Holy Crystal, your Superconductor combo deletes ranged carries. After Holy Crystal, it deletes everyone except dedicated tanks. Plan your second rotation around the timing: when the item finishes, look for a side lane where the enemy has used their escape, and force a kill before they retreat to base.\"}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The spike is wasted if you panic-buy Winter Crown ahead of Holy Crystal because you died once. You died because you walked too far up, not because you lacked defense. Buy Holy Crystal first; Winter Crown is a third or fourth slot, never a second.\"}]\n87:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-4\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight positioning and target priority\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The reflex when you see the enemy form up around their tank is to stand at max range and try to land Ball Lightning on the carry from across the screen. That reflex is wrong. Ball Lightning is not a sniper rifle, it is a mid-range mark that needs to land on someone whose silhouette your team is about to focus.\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Three rules:\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-1\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Stand at the back of your front line, not behind your back line.\"}],\" Your S2 cast range is shorter than most marksmen's basic-attack range. If you are positioned behind your carry, the enemy assassins will reach you before your tank reaches them. Sit behind your tank's silhouette so you cast Ball Lightning the instant the tank engages, and the bounce hits whoever the enemy clusters around.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Lead with S2 onto the enemy's most central target, not their highest-priority one.\"}],\" The bounce travels to nearby enemies. A Ball Lightning landed on the enemy tank in the middle of their formation bounces to two carries. The same skill landed on the back-line marksman bounces to nobody, because everyone else is too far away.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Hold ult for the second engage if the first engage is bait.\"}],\" Eudora's ultimate is on too long a cooldown for an \\\"always combo on entry\\\" pattern. If your tank's first engage is a single-target lock that the enemy walks out of, save the ult and the area follow-up for when both teams commit.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"If your support is Tigreal or Atlas, you get to cast Ball Lightning the moment they ult, because the entire enemy team is grouped and stunned. If your support is Estes or Rafaela, you have to create your own opening by waiting for an enemy to overextend into your team, which means longer game timer per fight.\"}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"$La5\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n8d:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: 3 locked slots, 3 real conversations\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Locked slots: \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Magic Boots\"}],\", \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Genius Wand\"}],\", \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Holy Crystal\"}],\". Magic Boots over Arcane Boots because the cooldown reduction matters more than 10 flat magic penetration once Genius Wand is online. Arcane Boots is fine if the enemy stacks magic defense early, but you are buying penetration twice in that case and one of those buys is a luxury.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The flex slots are where games are won. Walk through each:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",\"ul-0\",{\"className\":\"list-disc list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"vs grouped tanky comp\"}],\": rush Divine Glaive in slot 4. The Spellbreaker passive converts their magic defense into extra penetration, capped at 20 percent, which is exactly the counter to a team that has started stacking it. Buying Divine Glaive into a Khufra-Edith-Tigreal triple-front is the difference between your S1 tickling and your S1 killing.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"vs dive comp (Hayabusa, Helcurt, Karina, Saber)\"}],\": Winter Crown in slot 4. The 2-second untargetable active is your \\\"I survived the assassin's full combo\\\" button. Note that the item is \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Winter Crown\"}],\", not Winter Truncheon: it was renamed in patch 1.8.92 and the description in some older guides is out of date. Press it the moment you see the assassin animation start, not when your HP bar starts dropping.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"vs poke comp (Pharsa, Selena, Beatrix)\"}],\": Blood Wings in slot 5 or 6. The 800-base shield (plus 100 percent of total magic power) regenerates 20 seconds after taking damage, so if you can disengage from a poke trade for 20 seconds (which is what a poke comp wants you to do anyway) the shield is up for the next fight. The 90 magic power is incidental, the shield is the buy.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"vs comp where games end fast\"}],\": Wishing Lantern as the finishing item. The Butterfly Goddess passive triggers every 800 magic damage dealt and removes 10 percent of a target's current HP. Eudora dishes 800 magic damage in two skills against any squishy. The execute scales with their HP, not yours, so it stays relevant even if you die before it fires.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"The weakest common default is \",\"$La6\",\". It synergized with the old pre-revamp Clock of Destiny build, but post-rework Eudora's S1 already cycles fast enough that the Resonate proc (every 6 seconds) gates extra damage she would already have from the Superconductor bonus. Buy it as a sixth item only if the game is already won and you want a slightly larger nuke on a cleared wave.\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$La7\",\"\\n\",\"$La8\",\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\"]\n8e:[\"$\",\"$Lb2\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Eudora\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8f:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-14 h-14 rounded-full overflow-hidd